    },
    {
      "id": "reflection",
      "label": "",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "n207",
          "type": "kicker",
          "text": "WHAT WOULD I CHANGE?"
        },
        {
          "id": "n208",
          "type": "statement",
          "text": "If I had *more time*, I would've…"
        },
        {
          "id": "n209",
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "n210",
              "text": "spent longer *ideating wireframes* and app structure — specifically the organization of the library page."
            },
            {
              "id": "n211",
              "text": "explored this concept as an *integrated feature* within Spotify as opposed to an independent app."
            },
            {
              "id": "n212",
              "text": "conducted *more formalized research* — possibly a survey. Most of my user research was based on what I'd heard from friends or found online."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "n213",
          "type": "kicker",
          "text": "TAKEAWAYS"
        },
        {
          "id": "n214",
          "type": "takeaways",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "n215",
              "title": "First *Figma* experience",
              "body": "Picked up Figma in two weeks — going from using squares instead of frames to fully animated components, relying on advice from mentors and YouTube tutorials."
            },
            {
              "id": "n216",
              "title": "First *UI/UX case study* experience",
              "body": "Learned everything about case studies. Navigated brainstorming, user research, and iterations while learning how to create lo-fi and hi-fi prototypes."
            },
            {
              "id": "n217",
              "title": "User Research: Designing with *empathy*",
              "body": "I realized that design is about much more than how aesthetically pleasing something looks. Every aspect of a product must have intention and care behind it to truly improve users' lives."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
